  "id": "COMPOUND:22170 - PROTEIN:6078",
  "verbalization": "Ulongapeptin is implicated in the regulation of Forkhead box protein O1 (FoxO1) through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Ulongapeptin targets the Inner centromere protein, which in turn is a target of various compounds, including Epicatechin-(4beta->6)-epicatechin-(4beta->8)-catechin and 2-Hexulosonic acid. These compounds, in turn, are linked to FoxO1 through their respective targets. While the exact mechanism by which these compounds interact with FoxO1 remains unclear, the shared pathway from Ulongapeptin to the Inner centromere protein and then to FoxO1 indicates a potential regulatory relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the Inner centromere protein as a central node in the signaling network, suggesting that Ulongapeptin may influence FoxO1 through this intermediate. The evidence supports a plausible but indirect connection between Ulongapeptin and FoxO1, emphasizing the importance of the Inner centromere protein in mediating this relationship.",
